    "title": "Fallen Alaksa firefighter honored in procession | Local & State News | fox21online.com",
    "text": "MINNESOTA (KQDS-TV) -- A procession was held to honor a firefighter who died near Ely on August 11.\nLeslie R. Washington was a firefighter from Alaska. He was part of the \"K-River 2\" from Scorched Earth Services, a crew that specializes in wildfire response. The team came to Minnesota to aid in the wildfire fight in and around the Boundary Waters. Washington was working on the Bear Trap fire near Ely when he died.\nMore information is expected to be released at a later time.",
